{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791635316,"nonce":"Yt6xYmjaABzezwDXAz5PrQ4FIg0=","title":"Null-initialised locals have no monomorph, so macro typeof reports Dynamic","message":"Conformance rows Issue2776 and Issue3396 (macro typeof fidelity).\n\n- Issue2776: `var type = null; switch (type) { case String: case Int: }` should type\n  `type` as Null\u003cClass\u003cmono\u003e\u003e (Null\u003cEnum\u003cmono\u003e\u003e for enum cases); rayzor gives Dynamic.\n  On the expected side an unbound generic return prints `TInst(T,[])` where Haxe prints\n  a monomorph. `typeError(switch ... case String: case ExprDef:)` must error (mixed\n  class/enum cases) and does not.\n- Issue3396: `var r = null` read inside a closure before any assignment stays Dynamic\n  (null_read_in_closure). Haxe binds r's monomorph to String through the closure's\n  return at `var s:String = f([])`, and reports Null\u003cString\u003e.\n\nSuggested direction: in type_expr_in_scope, map out-of-scope type parameters to\nunknown_type (prints TMono); record Null\u003cClass\u003cUnknown\u003e\u003e/Null\u003cEnum\u003cUnknown\u003e\u003e for a\nnull-inferred switch subject in the macro_source_types side table (added for\nIssue7672); raise a SemanticError on mixed class/enum cases. Issue3396 needs real\nmonomorphs for null locals.","files":null}]}